From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: drm/vc4: Give the BCM2712 DRM device a 36-bit DMA mask

Since the stable merge of "drm/vc4: Set DRM DMA device directly from
HVS and V3D", only the HVS gets the 36-bit mask. In 6.18 drm_gem_dma
allocates on drm->dev. On BCM2712 that device is behind the HVS IOMMU,
which maps at 0xa00000000. With a 32-bit mask every buffer fails with
-ENOMEM: no fbdev console and no dumb buffers, so HDMI stays dark.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -356,6 +356,14 @@ static int vc4_drm_bind(struct device *dev)
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
 		}
+	} else if (gen >= VC4_GEN_6_C) {
+		/*
+		 * drm_gem_dma allocates on drm->dev in 6.18. On BCM2712 that
+		 * device is behind the HVS IOMMU, which maps above 4 GiB.
+		 */
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(36));
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
 
 	vc4 = devm_drm_dev_alloc(dev, driver, struct vc4_dev, base);
